  "notes": "COMMON COLLOCATIONS:\nSense 1:\n- ショートヘア: short hair\n- ショートカット: short haircut (note: not used for computer shortcuts as in English)\n- ショートケーキ: shortcake (Japanese-style strawberry sponge cake)\n- ショートパンツ: shorts\n- ショートフィルム: short film\n\nSense 2:\n- ショートする: to short-circuit\n- ショート{回路|かいろ}: short circuit\n\nCAUTION:\nJapanese ショートケーキ refers to a strawberry sponge cake with whipped cream, which is different from what \"shortcake\" means in American English (a biscuit-based dessert).\n\nショートカット in Japanese typically means a short hairstyle for women, not a keyboard shortcut or a shorter route.",
